Wrapper class

wrapper classes provide an object representation of primitive values.
They will also provide useful methods for working with those values.

byte -Byte
short -Short
int - Integer
long - Long
float - Float
double - Double
boolean - Boolean
char - Character

Example : to convert the primitve to an object 
int x=10;//primitve
Integer intObj=Integer.valueOf(x);
Double dObj=Double


1..AutoBoxing 

automatic conversion of a primitive value into its corresponding wrapper class object.

example : int ->Integer 
		  byte -> Byte

2..AutoUnBoxing or unboxing

Automatic conversion of a wrapper class object into its corresponding primitive value..
example : Integer - >int
		  Byte -> byte 
